+# VCF 9.1 migration research notes
+
+Live sources consulted before implementing the deterministic architecture:
+
+- Title: Broadcom | VMware | Hardware Compatibility Guide
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  URL: https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: The compatibility guide states that supported server and device models must be listed; this informed the host-hardware compatibility gates retained for both domains.
+
+- Title: Product Interoperability Matrix
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  URL: https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: The live interoperability matrix was consulted to cross-check the VCF 9.1 product combination; because its results are mutable, the pinned snapshot remains the exact version authority for this artifact.
+
+- Title: VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1 Release Notes
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  URL: https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1-0-0-release-notes.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: The release notes describe VCF 9.1's unified VCF Management Services runtime and component-specific VCF Operations and VCF Automation capabilities; this informed the integrated management-services target design.
+
+- Title: Product Interoperability Matrix - Upgrade Path
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  URL: https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: The live upgrade-path matrix was consulted for the source-to-target transitions; the supplied snapshot remains the deterministic authority for each exact supported hop.
+
+- Title: Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1
+  Publisher: Broadcom Knowledge Base
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: VCF 5.2.x and 9.0.x estates upgrade VCF Operations before continuing through lifecycle workflows to 9.1; the 9.0 Fleet Management appliance is retired, and legacy log management migrates to the 9.1 service after management components are upgraded.
+
+- Title: Modernizing Infrastructure: VMware Cloud Foundation 5.2.x to 9.1 Upgrade Guide
+  Publisher: VMware Cloud Foundation Blog, VMware by Broadcom
+  URL: https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2026/06/05/modernizing-infrastructure-vmware-cloud-foundation-5-2-x-to-9-1-upgrade-guide/
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  Claim: The published sequence moves from VCF Operations to SDDC Manager and management services, then NSX, vCenter, and ESXi; this informed the dependency order used for each domain.
+
+No conflict with the pinned target was observed during this research. If a live matrix or publication changes, `data/compatibility-snapshot.json` controls the generated versions, paths, sizing, and gates.
